WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

02:05.270 --> 02:08.110
<b>Mom, there’s something outside.</b>

02:08.110 --> 02:10.070
<b>Hey, Mom...</b>

02:10.080 --> 02:11.580
<b>It’s just a cat.</b>

02:11.580 --> 02:13.080
<b>It isn’t a cat...</b>

02:13.080 --> 02:15.310
<b>Now, now, it’s time for bed.</b>

02:15.310 --> 02:18.050
<b>What book should I read you tonight?</b>

02:18.550 --> 02:25.550
<b>The End of a Forlorn and Plentiful Winter</b>

02:27.790 --> 02:29.560
<b>Kisa...</b>

02:29.560 --> 02:31.900
<b>Why?</b>

02:31.900 --> 02:33.960
<b>Why do things like this happen?</b>

02:53.320 --> 02:54.250
<b>Rieko-chan!</b>

02:57.560 --> 02:59.720
<b>Why are you here, too?</b>

03:00.890 --> 03:02.790
<b>Private reasons.</b>

03:02.790 --> 03:04.400
<b>Okay. Understood.</b>

03:04.400 --> 03:10.870
<b>Then... I’d appreciate it if you could
at least tell me what’s going on.</b>

03:10.870 --> 03:13.000
<b>They’re gone...</b>

03:13.000 --> 03:15.410
<b>Dosshiru and Shisshin.</b>

03:15.410 --> 03:16.670
<b>Pou-chan, too.</b>

03:16.680 --> 03:17.680
<b>Pou-chan?</b>

03:22.050 --> 03:25.120
<b>After I’ve been called here,
you’re going to run from me again?</b>

03:25.120 --> 03:29.150
<b>I want to leave those two alone right now.</b>

03:29.150 --> 03:31.190
<b>Oh, in the middle of adolescence, are they?</b>

03:41.030 --> 03:45.040
<b>I’m... no good.</b>

03:47.640 --> 03:49.310
<b>You think so?</b>

03:49.310 --> 03:54.280
<b>I do nothing but bring trouble to you and Riezo.</b>

03:54.280 --> 03:58.180
<b>And now Bun-chan and Pou-chan
are gone because of me.</b>

03:58.180 --> 04:04.260
<b>It’s not like Bun-chan and Pou-chan
left you because they wanted to.</b>

04:04.260 --> 04:08.230
<b>And... I’m here now, as is Riezo.</b>

04:09.690 --> 04:14.870
<b>One day... you two will surely leave me, too.</b>

04:14.870 --> 04:16.670
<b>You’ll come to hate me.</b>

04:22.210 --> 04:23.570
<b>I’m sorry...</b>

04:23.580 --> 04:26.080
<b>Why are you apologizing?</b>

04:26.080 --> 04:27.110
<b>Get up.</b>

04:27.110 --> 04:28.650
<b>The ground is cold, isn’t it?</b>

04:29.710 --> 04:32.920
<b>Come on, is this really what
you wish to do?</b>

04:32.920 --> 04:34.290
<b>Wish?</b>

04:34.290 --> 04:38.420
<b>Kisa, what do you want to do?
What do you want to become?</b>

04:41.030 --> 04:43.860
<b>You... always ask these kinds of questions, Shigeki.</b>

04:45.400 --> 04:48.470
<b>“What do you want to do?”
“What do you want to become?”</b>

04:48.470 --> 04:52.840
<b>Well, yeah... because that’s where everything begins.</b>

04:52.840 --> 04:56.970
<b>Shigeki, you say you want to become
a professional shogi player...</b>

04:56.980 --> 05:00.550
<b>...so you actually have a goal
to aim for, right?</b>

05:00.550 --> 05:05.050
<b>You’ve discovered exactly what you want to become.</b>

05:05.050 --> 05:06.620
<b>But...</b>

05:06.620 --> 05:10.790
<b>I really have no idea what I want to do.</b>

05:12.420 --> 05:17.130
<b>Because... I have nothing.</b>

05:22.100 --> 05:23.370
<b>Rieko-chan!</b>

05:26.300 --> 05:27.540
<b>Wait up!</b>

05:34.510 --> 05:36.480
<b>Are you all right?</b>

05:36.480 --> 05:37.520
<b>Makki...</b>

05:39.180 --> 05:40.380
<b>Let me... cry for a bit.</b>

05:40.920 --> 05:41.920
<b>Okay.</b>

05:51.700 --> 05:57.670
<b>Kokusaibashi Bridge</b>

05:53.730 --> 05:56.470
<b>I overlooked another crucial point, huh?</b>

05:58.270 --> 06:01.970
<b>You guys have seen both, right?</b>

06:01.970 --> 06:03.140
<b>Seen both what?</b>

06:03.140 --> 06:07.650
<b>Tonight’s fairies and Tanigawa-san’s evil disappearing.</b>

06:10.520 --> 06:16.890
<b>Hey, I heard the one she was keeping
turned into a fairy. Is that true?</b>

06:16.890 --> 06:18.120
<b>And if it was?</b>

06:18.120 --> 06:21.260
<b>Isn’t that kind of thing really important?</b>

06:23.200 --> 06:26.000
<b>What’s important to you, Sukawara-san?</b>

06:26.000 --> 06:29.130
<b>Reporting the truth, of course.</b>

06:29.130 --> 06:31.200
<b>This might sound kind of weird, but...</b>

06:31.200 --> 06:35.210
<b>...do you think the “truth” is something that
can be properly conveyed to everyone?</b>

06:36.410 --> 06:41.480
<b>Who do you think you’re asking?
I’m still a journalist.</b>

06:41.480 --> 06:42.610
<b>Yeah, that’s right.</b>

06:42.610 --> 06:44.920
<b>But I understand what you’re trying to say.</b>

06:46.220 --> 06:48.120
<b>I’ve also thought about it.</b>

06:48.120 --> 06:52.690
<b>For example, the news conveys
information on some disaster.</b>

06:52.690 --> 06:55.730
<b>There are many casualties,
and many people are missing.</b>

06:55.730 --> 06:59.760
<b>And just with those numbers,
we learn the extent of the disaster.</b>

06:59.770 --> 07:03.100
<b>But have we really learned what it is?</b>

07:04.040 --> 07:07.070
<b>That’s what you’re trying to say, right?</b>

07:07.070 --> 07:13.110
<b>The true meaning of what happened on the night
of the Cat Dance isn’t conveyed in your book.</b>

07:13.110 --> 07:16.550
<b>You’re really asking to be slugged, aren’t you?</b>

07:18.120 --> 07:20.090
<b>It’ll bother me if you do.</b>

07:20.090 --> 07:22.790
<b>I don’t intend to, anyway.</b>

07:22.790 --> 07:24.460
<b>With the disaster example...</b>

07:24.460 --> 07:28.060
<b>...the only ones who’ve felt its extent are
the victims and those who were there.</b>

07:28.060 --> 07:33.330
<b>Those sent to the scene to rescue survivors,
and those sent out to recover the corpses...</b>

07:33.330 --> 07:36.400
<b>Yes... unfortunately, it’s just as you say.</b>

07:36.400 --> 07:38.370
<b>Even if the numerical facts are extremely precise...</b>

07:38.370 --> 07:43.070
<b>...they’re nothing more than a copied, watered-
down version of what actually happened.</b>

07:43.070 --> 07:45.880
<b>Which is why we try to grasp the truth behind it all.</b>

07:45.880 --> 07:48.050
<b>That’s what I’m confused about.</b>

07:49.410 --> 07:52.350
<b>Is there really just one truth?</b>

07:52.350 --> 07:55.620
<b>Even if there are definite facts
about what’s happened...</b>

07:55.620 --> 07:59.660
<b>...isn’t the number of truths equal to the
number of people on the planet?</b>

07:59.660 --> 08:02.160
<b>Yes... one for each person.</b>

08:02.160 --> 08:04.930
<b>But if you think like that, then there’s
really no point in reporting anything.</b>

08:04.930 --> 08:08.930
<b>That’s why all we do is simply report
the unfabricated facts as the truth.</b>

08:08.930 --> 08:14.140
<b>After that, it’s just a matter of how close we
can get to the real truth behind those facts.</b>

08:14.140 --> 08:15.910
<b>That’s all it is.</b>

08:18.240 --> 08:23.110
<b>And once you get all of that information,
it then goes through your filter, doesn’t it?</b>

08:23.110 --> 08:29.250
<b>Can you honestly say that you’re not just picking the truths most convenient to you?</b>

08:29.250 --> 08:31.620
<b>Are you suggesting that I’m biased?</b>

08:38.360 --> 08:39.060
<b>Kisa...</b>

08:43.440 --> 08:47.710
<b>At the beginning... there might really be nothing.</b>

08:47.710 --> 08:54.450
<b>But that would make living too difficult, so I want to believe that something’s out there.</b>

08:54.450 --> 08:57.450
<b>So I’m clinging to shogi.</b>

09:00.190 --> 09:07.290
<b>Kisa, you say I have shogi,
but that’s <i>all</i> I have.</b>

09:12.260 --> 09:15.270
<b>Shigeki, you chose shogi, didn’t you?</b>

09:15.270 --> 09:20.200
<b>But I... can’t even choose something, so...</b>

09:20.210 --> 09:22.140
<b>No, you did.</b>

09:26.910 --> 09:29.650
<b>Okay... I’m fine now.</b>

09:30.150 --> 09:31.320
<b>Here you go.</b>

09:31.320 --> 09:33.020
<b>Thank you.</b>

09:39.830 --> 09:43.090
<b>Makki, if only you were a girl...</b>

09:43.100 --> 09:47.830
<b>No... I wouldn’t want a girl version of me around.</b>

09:47.830 --> 09:50.940
<b>You’re able to compose yourself easily,
so I think you’d make a pretty good girl.</b>

09:50.940 --> 09:55.670
<b>If I were a girl... I don’t think I’d be friends with you.</b>

09:56.940 --> 09:59.510
<b>It’s just a hunch, but that’s how I feel.</b>

10:01.650 --> 10:03.710
<b>You may have been...</b>

10:05.120 --> 10:08.790
<b>...reluctant about writing your book as you did...</b>

10:08.790 --> 10:12.060
<b>...but I think it’s good that it was
written as a work of fiction.</b>

10:13.490 --> 10:17.960
<b>Even if that’s your truth, it’s different from mine.</b>

10:19.260 --> 10:21.670
<b>So you know something I don’t.</b>

10:21.670 --> 10:22.430
<b>I do.</b>

10:22.430 --> 10:23.100
<b>What is it?</b>

10:25.040 --> 10:26.570
<b>Wakkun.</b>

10:26.570 --> 10:30.540
<b>Then... what did I choose?</b>

10:30.540 --> 10:32.980
<b>To become involved with Bun-chan.</b>

10:34.950 --> 10:39.850
<b>You... still haven’t abandoned that, right?</b>

10:43.290 --> 10:45.990
<b>Why do you think that?
What do you mean?</b>

10:45.990 --> 10:50.050
<b>I’d probably find you annoying if I were the same type of girl as you...</b>

10:50.050 --> 10:52.760
<b>...because you’re always in the spotlight.</b>

10:54.000 --> 10:55.500
<b>Annoying?</b>

10:55.500 --> 10:58.170
<b>Sorry, but that’s just the feeling I get.</b>

10:58.170 --> 10:58.970
<b>And...</b>

10:58.970 --> 11:00.910
<b>And what?</b>

11:00.910 --> 11:03.980
<b>Tanigawa is the opposite of you.
She’s always in the shadows.</b>

11:03.980 --> 11:07.850
<b>But whichever side you two were on, I think something would still work out between you.</b>

11:07.850 --> 11:10.920
<b>Between me and Kisa?</b>

11:12.120 --> 11:14.820
<b>Could it be that Wakkun’s... the kappa?</b>

11:14.820 --> 11:16.320
<b>No.</b>

11:16.320 --> 11:18.890
<b>And I don’t intend to tell you about it.</b>

11:18.890 --> 11:21.690
<b>Can you explain just what we are?</b>

11:21.690 --> 11:23.590
<b>That sure was out of the blue.</b>

11:23.600 --> 11:25.600
<b>In that context...</b>

11:25.600 --> 11:30.470
<b>...primates that have evolved from other mammals wouldn’t be the right answer, huh?</b>

11:30.470 --> 11:33.300
<b>The truth you’re seeking, Sukawara-san...</b>

11:33.310 --> 11:38.910
<b>“Isn’t it just a simple explanation that allows
people to think they know everything?”</b>

11:38.910 --> 11:40.880
<b>You know, Sukawara-san...</b>

11:40.880 --> 11:43.610
<b>Bun-chan and Pou-chan...</b>

11:47.550 --> 11:49.220
<b>You’re saying we’re the same...?</b>

11:50.290 --> 11:53.390
<b>They’re the same... so this is...</b>

11:53.390 --> 11:55.460
<b>This is not a battle.</b>

12:04.840 --> 12:06.570
<b>What’s all this?</b>

12:13.750 --> 12:23.450
<b>This isn’t the battle between light and darkness
or good and evil like everyone’s thinking...</b>

12:23.460 --> 12:26.020
<b>If it isn’t a battle, what is it?</b>

12:26.020 --> 12:30.500
<b>Umm... we’re all looking for our other selves, I think.</b>

12:30.500 --> 12:34.300
<b>Our “other selves”? You mean like the term
in that weird ninja cloning technique?</b>

12:34.300 --> 12:35.530
<b>Yeah.</b>

12:35.530 --> 12:38.170
<b>The reason Bun-chan became attached to me...</b>

12:38.170 --> 12:42.510
<b>...and the reason Pou-chan was born from
that object was because I wanted it.</b>

12:42.510 --> 12:46.040
<b>Because you felt the need for them?</b>

12:46.040 --> 12:49.810
<b>Yes... sort of... but it’s a little different.</b>

12:52.880 --> 12:55.820
<b>Ahh... how can I say this?</b>

12:55.820 --> 12:57.590
<b>My words...</b>

12:59.020 --> 13:00.790
<b>You can explain slowly.</b>

13:00.790 --> 13:01.730
<b>Okay.</b>

13:02.790 --> 13:06.830
<b>You’re saying that Bun-chan and
Pou-chan are your other selves?</b>

13:06.830 --> 13:08.430
<b>There’s that, but...</b>

13:09.940 --> 13:13.040
<b>...my real other self is elsewhere.</b>

13:13.040 --> 13:14.410
<b>She’s on that side...</b>

13:17.210 --> 13:18.840
<b>I see...</b>

13:18.840 --> 13:27.080
<b>Because I wished for it, Bun-chan and Pou-chan
came over to this side... they came for me.</b>

13:28.720 --> 13:31.120
<b>Sorry, I can’t understand that.</b>

13:32.260 --> 13:35.220
<b>This place is seriously
looking dangerous...</b>

13:35.220 --> 13:37.660
<b>...so don’t you think we should head underground to escape?</b>

13:37.660 --> 13:40.330
<b>Enough of that!
Answer me.</b>

13:40.330 --> 13:42.930
<b>Why did you lump the two of us together?</b>

13:42.930 --> 13:46.440
<b>I’m sorry... that’s not how I meant it.</b>

13:46.440 --> 13:47.810
<b>But you just...</b>

13:47.810 --> 13:50.310
<b>I’ll explain my reasoning.</b>

13:51.140 --> 13:56.480
<b>Umm... recently, you’ve been
a little different, Rieko-chan.</b>

13:56.480 --> 13:59.950
<b>You never used to show your
annoyance to anyone, right?</b>

13:59.950 --> 14:01.890
<b>That’s what they call maturity.</b>

14:01.890 --> 14:06.760
<b>Yeah. I thought that was required to be an adult, too.</b>

14:06.760 --> 14:10.160
<b>Which is why I didn’t want to become one.</b>

14:10.160 --> 14:12.800
<b>Makes sense for you, Makki.</b>

14:12.800 --> 14:17.770
<b>If holding yourself back is what it means to
be an adult, then I’m an adult right now.</b>

14:17.770 --> 14:19.500
<b>Holding yourself back is necessary...</b>

14:19.500 --> 14:24.180
<b>...but now I believe that it’s not good
to hold yourself back all the time.</b>

14:25.210 --> 14:28.080
<b>I feel like... I sort of understand what you’re saying.</b>

14:28.080 --> 14:34.750
<b>Hey, I wonder where all the feelings
we force ourselves to hold back go?</b>

14:35.850 --> 14:36.720
<b>The feelings?</b>

14:37.560 --> 14:39.560
<b>That’s how Tanigawa-san’s
the same as you.</b>

14:39.560 --> 14:44.700
<b>I wonder where all of her overflowing
negative feelings go?</b>

14:49.730 --> 14:54.670
<b>You’re right. I thought the two types
of lights were opposing each other.</b>

14:54.670 --> 14:58.480
<b>I suppose you could call that a bias.</b>

14:58.480 --> 15:03.320
<b>But to suddenly say “this is not a battle”
because of that is a little...</b>

15:03.320 --> 15:07.950
<b>If this is a battle, I can’t explain what
happened with Tanigawa-san’s light.</b>

15:10.160 --> 15:14.690
<b>This isn’t the first time something like this
has happened. You said that on TV, right?</b>

15:14.690 --> 15:17.360
<b>I did. I think that way now, as well.</b>

15:17.360 --> 15:19.430
<b>I also think the same.</b>

15:19.430 --> 15:22.430
<b>The warm- and cold-colored fairies have
been around since ancient times...</b>

15:22.430 --> 15:25.540
<b>...and will be here far into the future.</b>

15:25.540 --> 15:30.780
<b>A hole opens in the world’s membrane and we
just happen to see through it now and then.</b>

15:30.780 --> 15:35.710
<b>I think this is almost
a natural phenomenon.</b>

15:35.710 --> 15:39.020
<b>Now you’re saying this is a natural phenomenon,
despite everything you’ve said before?</b>

15:39.020 --> 15:42.790
<b>I know thinking it’s a “natural phenomenon”
is a little reckless.</b>

15:42.790 --> 15:46.860
<b>But to give a similar example, there’s such
a thing called “annihilation,” right?</b>

15:46.860 --> 15:53.160
<b>You mean like when matter and antimatter or particles and antiparticles come into contact?</b>

15:53.160 --> 15:54.400
<b>Yeah.</b>

15:54.400 --> 15:59.300
<b>I’ve never seen it myself,
but I think it’s an ordinary thing...</b>

15:59.300 --> 16:02.040
<b>...and this situation is close to that.</b>

16:02.040 --> 16:04.340
<b>Wait one sec. Thinking...</b>

16:05.040 --> 16:08.080
<b>Then Acalanatha’s servants are the
same as the Tsukumogami?</b>

16:08.080 --> 16:10.120
<b>Is it wrong to say they’re all the same?</b>

16:10.120 --> 16:12.650
<b>No... it’s not, but...</b>

16:16.820 --> 16:19.160
<b>It was all... just me.</b>

16:21.860 --> 16:23.890
<b>This sure is incredible...</b>

16:23.890 --> 16:25.860
<b>This is something I’ll never forget.</b>

16:25.860 --> 16:27.630
<b>Hey, it looks like they’re all headed off that way.</b>

16:56.860 --> 17:00.470
<b>Light and shadow don’t battle each other...</b>

17:00.470 --> 17:02.800
<b>...because they’re two sides of the same coin.</b>

17:08.310 --> 17:13.180
<b>Our feelings... probably take shape and turn into that...</b>

17:16.880 --> 17:24.860
<b>Bun-chan and Pou-chan both
came to my place for me.</b>

17:38.670 --> 17:40.270
<b>This sure is a spectacle, huh?</b>

17:40.970 --> 17:43.740
<b>Oh, my. It looks like you’re still the same as always.</b>

17:43.740 --> 17:48.350
<b>I’m sure I’ll change now... in many ways.</b>

17:48.350 --> 17:50.080
<b>We’ll just have to see.</b>

17:51.020 --> 17:58.720
<b>This world is far more complicated,
rich and full of mystery than people think.</b>

17:58.720 --> 18:04.060
<b>After being shown something so unexpected,
I have no choice but to change.</b>

18:04.060 --> 18:08.600
<b>If that’s all you’re talking about,
people used to know that.</b>

18:08.600 --> 18:12.170
<b>We just forgot it.</b>

18:12.170 --> 18:16.410
<b>Can’t I use remembering something
as a trigger for change?</b>

18:18.280 --> 18:21.880
<b>You can’t just say you’ll change.
You actually have to.</b>

18:23.150 --> 18:26.120
<b>Yeah. I’m watching it on TV right now.</b>

18:26.120 --> 18:29.860
<b>I can see it from my place! It’s amazing!</b>

18:29.860 --> 18:32.860
<b>But... will your boyfriend be all right?</b>

18:33.330 --> 18:35.790
<b>Umm... I can’t get in touch with him.</b>

18:35.790 --> 18:38.530
<b>What? Then shouldn’t you be more worried?!</b>

18:38.530 --> 18:44.840
<b>Well... maybe a little deep down,
but I know he’ll be fine.</b>

18:44.840 --> 18:46.400
<b>I’m not worried.</b>

19:31.780 --> 19:36.190
<b>Umm... why did you call me here today?</b>

19:36.190 --> 19:38.290
<b>Do you think this is over?</b>

19:38.290 --> 19:40.660
<b>It isn’t?</b>

19:44.860 --> 19:47.260
<b>Our work really starts from this point on.</b>

19:47.260 --> 19:50.800
<b>I’m going to make a book out of it. This time I’m going to write about what happened here.</b>

19:50.800 --> 19:51.770
<b>I see.</b>

19:51.770 --> 19:53.740
<b>Don’t say “I see” like this were some trivial matter.</b>

19:55.110 --> 19:58.080
<b>Makabe-kun, do you want to read over
my manuscript once I’m done with it?</b>

19:58.080 --> 19:59.040
<b>Me?</b>

19:59.040 --> 20:03.850
<b>You’re an eyewitness, so I want you to read
it and play devil’s advocate for me.</b>

20:05.120 --> 20:06.080
<b>Okay!</b>

20:06.080 --> 20:08.320
<b>And... what happened to school?</b>

20:08.320 --> 20:11.060
<b>Today’s just the semester’s
closing ceremony.</b>

20:11.060 --> 20:12.790
<b>Even so, you should still go!</b>

20:12.790 --> 20:15.530
<b>No way! And you’re the one who
called me today, anyway...</b>

20:19.830 --> 20:20.500
<b>Hello?</b>

20:21.170 --> 20:24.700
<b>Ah, Kobayakawa? Will you be participating
in today’s shogi class?</b>

20:27.110 --> 20:28.800
<b>Shogi Institute</b>

20:27.110 --> 20:29.240
<b>Of course I will!</b>

20:29.240 --> 20:31.080
<b>I’m right outside.</b>

20:43.260 --> 20:43.960
<b>Hello?</b>

20:43.960 --> 20:47.160
<b>Ah, sorry. Were you still asleep?</b>

20:47.160 --> 20:49.230
<b>No, I was just waking up.</b>

20:49.230 --> 20:52.400
<b>Umm... I just wanted to thank you.</b>

20:53.570 --> 20:55.830
<b>I haven’t done anything.</b>

20:55.830 --> 20:59.870
<b>I only waited for you like an old friend did for me.</b>

21:01.010 --> 21:03.380
<b>You did say something like that before, didn’t you?</b>

21:03.380 --> 21:05.440
<b>Who is this “old friend”?</b>

21:05.440 --> 21:07.050
<b>Wakkun.</b>

21:07.050 --> 21:08.850
<b>The zashiki-warashi?</b>

21:07.050 --> 21:12.920
<b>[Note: A Japanese spirit, usually shown as
a small child who brings good fortune.]</b>

21:10.480 --> 21:12.920
<b>I guess that couldn’t be him.</b>

21:12.920 --> 21:17.860
<b>You see, when I was younger, I remember
playing a lot with a zashiki-warashi.</b>

21:17.860 --> 21:22.830
<b>I don’t really remember it, but everyone
says I named it “Wakkun.”</b>

21:24.000 --> 21:27.360
<b>Since it was a <i>wa</i>-rashi, I named it “Wakkun,” I guess.</b>

21:27.360 --> 21:28.800
<b>You couldn’t... have been in Tana?</b>

21:29.430 --> 21:31.640
<b>Tana? What’s that?</b>

21:31.640 --> 21:32.770
<b>A place.</b>

21:32.770 --> 21:34.640
<b>So it’s a place.</b>

21:34.640 --> 21:37.510
<b>Well, I played with him somewhere in Aomori,
but I can’t remember the name.</b>

21:37.510 --> 21:39.950
<b>If I remember correctly, it was
before I entered kindergarten.</b>

21:39.950 --> 21:42.210
<b>So you were in the Tohoku region...</b>

21:42.210 --> 21:47.180
<b>Yeah... did I say something weird?</b>

21:47.190 --> 21:50.220
<b>I was happy that you were waiting for me.</b>

21:50.220 --> 21:51.320
<b>Yeah.</b>

21:51.320 --> 21:52.220
<b>Thank you.</b>

21:55.430 --> 21:57.160
<b>The warashi, Wakkun?</b>

21:58.530 --> 22:00.730
<b>The zashiki-warashi of the Touya Forest?</b>

22:06.440 --> 22:07.440
<b>Good morning!</b>

22:07.440 --> 22:08.940
<b>You sure called early today.</b>

22:08.940 --> 22:10.040
<b>Just a little.</b>

22:10.780 --> 22:13.240
<b>There’s a lot of things I want to talk to you about.</b>

22:15.480 --> 22:17.010
<b>I guess I can handle that.</b>

22:17.010 --> 22:18.020
<b>Okay.</b>

22:19.350 --> 22:20.480
<b>Riezo!</b>

22:22.120 --> 22:23.020
<b>Good morning.</b>

22:24.720 --> 22:26.260
<b>What’s gotten into you?!</b>

22:26.260 --> 22:28.490
<b>I thought I’d go to school today.</b>

22:28.490 --> 22:31.430
<b>Even though today’s only the closing ceremony?</b>

22:31.430 --> 22:34.870
<b>I decided I’d go from now on,
so I’m going today.</b>

22:36.230 --> 22:37.970
<b>I don’t get you at times.</b>

22:42.310 --> 22:44.440
<b>Wearing this uniform in the winter sure is cold...</b>

22:44.440 --> 22:46.480
<b>High school girls become true high school girls...</b>

22:46.480 --> 22:48.910
<b>...once they lose all feeling in their legs at times like these.</b>

22:48.910 --> 22:51.620
<b>That’s impossible.
Completely impossible.</b>

22:51.620 --> 22:54.750
<b>It’s the punishment you get from
missing school all this time.</b>

22:55.750 --> 22:58.320
<b>Riezo, you’re really not cold?</b>

23:01.460 --> 23:04.060
<b>No... I am.</b>

23:11.370 --> 23:14.040
<b>Hey, why are you laughing? Kisa!</b>

23:22.080 --> 23:29.790
<b>The End</b>

23:32.230 --> 23:39.800
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

23:32.230 --> 23:39.800
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

23:39.800 --> 23:46.510
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

23:39.800 --> 23:46.510
words that no one else knew.

23:49.510 --> 23:57.010
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:49.510 --> 23:57.010
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:57.010 --> 24:03.690
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:57.010 --> 24:03.690
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

24:03.690 --> 24:11.130
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

24:03.690 --> 24:11.130
Ah, I thought that being alone

24:11.130 --> 24:15.930
Sore de ii to omotta

24:11.130 --> 24:15.930
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

24:15.930 --> 24:24.610
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

24:15.930 --> 24:24.610
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

24:24.610 --> 24:33.210
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

24:24.610 --> 24:33.210
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

24:33.210 --> 24:41.990
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

24:33.210 --> 24:41.990
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:41.990 --> 24:50.700
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:41.990 --> 24:50.700
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:50.700 --> 24:59.240
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:50.700 --> 24:59.240
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

25:00.010 --> 25:03.110
<b>And so, Zettai Shonen is over.</b>

25:03.120 --> 25:04.320
<b>It’s over?</b>

25:04.320 --> 25:05.490
<b>It looks like it is...</b>

25:05.490 --> 25:09.190
<b>Taruto! Taruto! Where did you go?</b>

25:09.190 --> 25:12.460
<b>Ah! Nene-chan is calling for me! I’m going now!</b>

25:12.460 --> 25:16.390
<b>Hey, Roku! Roku! Where are you?</b>

25:16.390 --> 25:19.630
<b>Heigorou-san’s calling for me, too. I have to go.</b>

25:19.630 --> 25:22.730
<b>Well then... where does that leave me to go home to?</b>

25:22.730 --> 25:26.440
<b>Old Lady Okaka! Old Lady Okaka,
where are you hiding?!</b>

25:26.440 --> 25:29.440
<b>Oh, it’s Ryousuke! He was still chasing after me?</b>

25:29.440 --> 25:32.180
<b>I won’t let you get away today, Old Lady Okaka!</b>

25:32.180 --> 25:35.350
<b>You’re too naive, Ryousuke!
I won’t be caught that easily.</b>

25:36.580 --> 25:39.720
<b>The End!</b>
